Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:41:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] macOS: NEO's system calls over xemac, the user side of
 IntelXe.kext

The Linux DRM/xe backend is built unchanged: every call it makes to the
kernel goes through NEO::SysCalls, and sys_calls_macos.cpp replaces
sys_calls_linux.cpp. The render node is IntelXe.kext's xe interface
(Linux's xe uAPI behind an IOUserClient), reached through xemac:

- open("/dev/dri/renderD128") is xemac_open(); /dev/dri/by-path does
  not exist, so Drm::discoverDevices tries the renderD nodes in turn and
  finds the one device. XEMAC_FAKE=1 gives xemac's canned Battlemage.
- ioctl, mmap, munmap and close of that fd go to xemac. The request
  numbers are those drm.h/xe_drm.h encode on a BSD system
  (<sys/ioccom.h>), which the kext decodes.
- /sys/dev/char/226:128 -> ../../devices/.../0000:bb:dd.f/drm/renderD128
  is synthesized from the kext's PCI identity, so getPciPath() works;
  readlink("/proc/self/exe") is answered with proc_pidpath() (AIL).
- prctl, pidfd_open and pidfd_getfd fail with ENOSYS; dlinfo
  (RTLD_DI_LINKMAP) walks dyld's image list; mremap(MREMAP_FIXED) and
  MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE are Mach VM calls; SOCK_CLOEXEC is FD_CLOEXEC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
